From 2526091a856dc4bc36aad4172866d2810fa6b633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:40:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] always-on roll: paused turns wait for the warming
 successor; proxy keeps half-closed responses; fenced reaper

Review 5878814630 of #1611 (t_01a1d0b9223dd165):

B1: a turn paused for a core update on an always-on backend gave up at
update_pause.HANDOFF_WAIT_S (90 s) while its successor was still booting and
warming, continued on stale code, and the roller's 900 s backstop could
SIGTERM it mid-turn.
- The superseded watchdog polls every 2 s (10 s while a live turn refuses the
  fence), so an idle superseded backend retires seconds after the switch.
- web_server_skew_exit.successor_pending(): true while active.json shows a roll
  in flight (another port warming) or already switched away. While it holds,
  _leave_decision skips HANDOFF_WAIT_S and the in-place backstop is
  SUCCESSOR_WARMING_GRACE_S (420 s) instead of LEAVE_GRACE_S. A busy backend
  still continues after NO_REPLACEMENT_S as before.
- reap_superseded retires through the backend's own idle fence
  (/api/health/retirement prepare+commit) after the grace and only SIGTERMs
  after 6 h; its clock is persisted in superseded.json so a roller restart
  (every core update) no longer resets it.

B2: Proxy._pipe closed its writer right after write_eof, so a client that
half-closed after its request got an empty response. _pipe now only
half-closes; handle closes both sockets once both directions finish (or one
breaks).

Nits: pick_port adopts a still-booting backend the previous roll left warming;
the roll re-checks unit + health before switching; supervise survives a bad
poll; _http_get catches http.client.HTTPException; malformed hour_epoch is
skipped; Proxy.target keys its cache on (st_ino, st_mtime_ns); replay_paths
docstring says two hours; the dashboard_procs test patches _on_linux and
route_always_on_backends instead of sys.platform/__kwdefaults__.
